{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aacacd0da0bf2a9b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9003\n3\ttitle: Reduce default workbench idle culling timeout to 8 hours\n4\tstatus: Refinement Done\n5\tpriority: Normal\n6\tlabels:\n7\t- refined\n8\tlinks: []\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## Problem Statement\n12\t\n13\tThe default workbench idle culling timeout ships at 24 hours, so abandoned\n14\tworkbenches hold GPUs overnight and through weekends. Fleet telemetry shows the\n15\tmedian idle-before-stop window admins actually configure is 8 hours. New\n16\tclusters should get the sensible default without an admin having to find the\n17\tsetting.\n18\t\n19\t## High-Level Requirements\n20\t\n21\t| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n22\t|-------|----------|-------------|\n23\t| HLR-1 | P1 | The default idle culling timeout for newly installed clusters is 8 hours instead of 24. Existing clusters with an explicitly configured value are not changed on upgrade. |\n24\t| HLR-2 | P2 | The release note and cluster-settings documentation state the new default and how to override it. |\n25\t\n26\t## Affected Components\n27\t\n28\t- Notebooks\n29\t- Dashboard\n30\t\n31\t## Out of Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Per-project or per-user culling policies\n34\t- Changes to activity detection (kernel probe behavior)\n35\t\n36\t## Open Questions\n37\t\n38\tNone — the setting, its ConfigMap, and the Dashboard administration UI already\n39\texist; only the shipped default changes.\n40\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0890903135805c5","agent_id":"a88f9f17c95434ffc","session_id":"ffa45458-1db1-4c5f-844c-4803ebe05acb","uuid":"5460f7f1-b1ec-4966-a5d6-c79aefb2e4d5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:17:42.323Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aacacd0da0bf2a9b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9003 decomposition"}
