{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0c2bbb3b46c6c1d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9003-E001\n3\ttitle: Reduce default workbench idle culling timeout to 8 hours\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9003\n5\tcomponent: Notebooks\n6\tteam: Workbenches\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Reduce default workbench idle culling timeout to 8 hours\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tChange the shipped default workbench idle culling timeout from 24 hours to 8 hours so that newly installed clusters reclaim idle GPU-held workbenches without an admin having to discover and change the setting. The culling setting, its ConfigMap, and the Dashboard administration UI already exist; only the shipped default value changes. Explicitly configured values on existing clusters must be preserved on upgrade. The epic also covers the release note and cluster-settings documentation update that states the new default and how to override it.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Change the shipped default idle culling timeout for workbenches from 24 hours to 8 hours in the culler configuration surface (the existing culling ConfigMap / default administered through the Dashboard's notebook-controller settings).\n38\t- Ensure the new default applies only to clusters where no explicit culling timeout is configured: existing clusters with an explicitly configured value are not changed on upgrade.\n39\t- Update the release note and the cluster-settings documentation to state the new 8-hour default and how to override it (the override mechanism and its documentation already exist; only the stated default changes).\n40\t- No changes to per-project or per-user culling policies.\n41\t- No changes to activity detection (kernel probe behavior).\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- Given a newly installed cluster with no explicitly configured idle culling timeout, when a workbench is idle, then it is culled after 8 hours of inactivity (the effective shipped default is 8 hours, not 24).\n46\t- Given a cluster upgraded from a previous release that has an explicitly configured idle culling timeout, when the upgrade completes, then the explicitly configured value is unchanged.\n47\t- Given the release notes and cluster-settings documentation, when the change ships, then they state the new 8-hour default and describe how to override it.\n48\t- Given a cluster running the new shipped default, when an admin opens the existing Dashboard administration UI for the notebook-controller culling settings, then the culling setting is still surfaced correctly and reflects the new 8-hour default.\n49\t- Culling behavior for activity detection (kernel probes) and per-workbench override semantics are unchanged from the previous release.\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- **HLR-1 (P1)**: The default idle culling timeout for newly installed clusters is 8 hours instead of 24; existing clusters with an explicitly configured value are not changed on upgrade. Covered by the default-value change and the upgrade-preservation scope above.\n54\t- **HLR-2 (P2)**: The release note and cluster-settings documentation state the new default and how to override it. Covered by the documentation update scope above.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba651a182dd6b600","agent_id":"a2bea26089cc32b8f","session_id":"ffa45458-1db1-4c5f-844c-4803ebe05acb","uuid":"af1a960d-1f16-4196-82ad-cf86c1271ed2"